{
  "configuration_id": "config_029",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_004: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat → 61.9% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality actually contributes meaningful signal over RNA alone. config_029 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to config_004: the RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation are all identical; only the image modality is removed. If RNA alone achieves comparable accuracy, it would collapse the search space by eliminating the need to optimize image encoders, fusion strategies, and cross-modal aggregation—saving many experiments. If RNA alone is substantially worse, it confirms multimodal fusion is essential and justifies investing subsequent experiments in encoder and fusion choices. Establishing this modality-level baseline before exploring encoder variants (scvi, scgpt, ViT-L) or fusion strategies (weighted, transformer) is the highest-information use of the next budget slot."
}

